WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.091
Cancelled cameos, deleted droids, and headless
humanoids are just some of the things that

00:00:05.091 --> 00:00:06.830
didn't make the final cut of Rogue One.

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:10.509
In this video, I'm going to break down the
movie's deleted scenes and characters and

00:00:10.509 --> 00:00:13.410
examine the reshoots and rumours and what
they meant for the film.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:17.150
There are also some really interesting rejected
concepts which I'll be looking at too.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.580
Of course, there are spoilers ahead for Rogue
One and anything Star Wars related, so be

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:25.020
aware of that, and if you're not ready then
make sure you see the movie first or check

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.210
out my spoiler-free video by tapping up here.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:32.279
When Industrial Light &amp; Magic's chief creative
officer John Knoll pitched his original Rogue

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:37.149
One concept, he put forward a line-up of characters
that was vastly different to the final team

00:00:37.149 --> 00:00:38.390
we see in the movie.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:42.801
The original title was going to be "Destroyer
of Worlds" and, as well as humans, the rebel

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:46.699
crew included two alien characters called
Lunak and Senna.

00:00:46.699 --> 00:00:51.710
Lunak and Senna went through multiple versions
of design during development, with Senna initially

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:56.559
depicted as a Chewbacca-style alien and Lunak
as a kind of side-kick who "could skitter

00:00:56.559 --> 00:00:59.140
into an air duct, almost like a little thief".

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:03.410
The aliens were later replaced with the Jedha
duo Chirrut Imwe and Baze Malbus, although

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:08.420
later designs of Senna appear to be the basis
for the mercenary Moroff who fights with Saw

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:09.689
Gerrera's Partisans.

00:01:09.689 --> 00:01:15.090
The other original Rogue One team members
were Jyn Erso, K-2SO, Dray Nevis, Ria Talla

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.760
and Jerris Kestal.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:21.710
Also during this early concept period, Krennic
was actually an imperial spy who had infiltrated

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:26.010
the team, sending back his intelligence to
an imperial officer called Willix Cree.

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:30.110
As well as changing the original characters,
the concept for Rogue One changed from an

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:34.730
ensemble action movie to one with more emphasis
on Jyn as the central character.

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:38.840
However, it seems by the final cut of the
movie, Jyn's role and screentime were pared

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:39.910
back somewhat.

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:44.090
The trailers point to these cuts with various
exchanges between Jyn, General Draven and

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:46.700
Mon Mothma deleted from the final movie.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:50.899
Including Mon Mothma's line "On your own from
the age of fifteen, reckless, aggressive and

00:01:50.899 --> 00:01:51.899
undisciplined."

00:01:51.899 --> 00:01:55.320
And there are also some snippets of snarky
dialogue from the trailers that were cut from

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:58.829
the final film, one of which was Jyn's line
"I rebel."

00:01:58.829 --> 00:02:02.560
The words proved unpopular with some fans
who felt the dialogue was a bit too on the

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:06.700
nose, and it's been rumoured that one objective
of the reshoots was to make Jyn's character

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:08.550
less antagonistic.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:13.140
Key to Jyn's partially missing backstory is
what appear to be some significant deleted

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.390
scenes with Saw Gerrera.

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:18.780
In the Celebration sizzle reel, there's a
deleted scene where Jyn and Saw are outside.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.880
Notice that Saw is bald at this point like
he is at the start of the movie when he rescues

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:26.950
the young Jyn, rather than grey haired as
he is when Jyn meets him in his cave in the

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:31.520
final movie, which suggests the cut scene
is a few years before the main timeline of

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:32.580
Rogue One.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:37.640
We know that Saw abandoned Jyn when she was
16 as he feared for her safety among his fellow

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:42.050
Partisans, so could this shot be showing that
very moment he left her which they talk about

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:43.130
in the movie?

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:47.010
The first trailer also shows a deleted scene
with a bald Saw Gerrera and also features

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:48.510
a speech he gives to Jyn.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:51.960
[Saw Gerrera] "What will you do when they
catch you?

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:54.324
What will you do if they break you?

00:02:54.324 --> 00:02:58.320
If you continue to fight, what will you become?"

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.970
And it seems like these words that we never
hear in the final movie, and which seem to

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:07.110
imply she was fighting alongside Saw, may
have given further background to why Saw abandoned

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:08.730
Jyn when she was a teenager.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:13.460
Remember, Saw Gerrera was considered an extremist,
with the Rebel Alliance cutting ties with

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:17.480
him, so perhaps the idea for cutting out this
part of Jyn's backstory was to make her a

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:19.540
more sympathetic character.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:24.360
Rumours have also surfaced of a deleted scene
between Saw Gerrera and Darth Vader.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:28.150
The rumour claims there's a scene where Darth
Vader attacks Saw Gerrera, badly injuring

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:29.550
the Rebel fighter.

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:34.230
And it's also claimed that there is another
cut scene where Vader smashes a Jedi temple.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:39.680
Both these claims are currently unsubstantiated,
but if true, they hint towards an even darker

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:42.290
and more violent Vader than we already saw
in Rogue One.

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:45.480
There are some Darth Vader scenes from the
trailers though that were definitely cut from

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:46.640
the final movie.

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:50.660
There's a cool shot of Vader looking on at
a red schematic of possibly the Death Star

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:55.970
plans, another foreboding reflection of his
image set against a fiery red planet or star,

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:59.600
and there's a cut scene where Krennic tells
Vader "the power we are dealing with here

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:00.840
is immeasurable".

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:05.050
What we see in the background of these scenes,
as well as an officially released promo still,

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:09.710
suggests that before the reshoots, Vader might
also have appeared on the Death Star in addition

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:10.800
to Mustafar.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.920
By the way, there were also rumours of a deleted
scene where Darth Vader hunted down three

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:18.880
of the main characters and killed them, and
I wonder whether this shot of a TIE fighter

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.790
appearing at the top of the antenna tower
could have been Vader arriving to take out

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.370
Jyn, Cassian and Krennic personally?

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:29.340
The scenes on Scarif are certainly a part
of the movie were we can see numerous scenes

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:32.950
that were cut from the trailers, which suggests
there was some significant reworking of the

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:34.970
story in the third act.

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:38.850
The transmission of the data tapes to the
Rebel Alliance appears to have been reworked

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:39.850
substantially.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:44.000
The first trailer has Jyn and her crew running
through the Citadel carrying the data tapes

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:48.290
and in another shot they are dodging enemy
fire from Stormtroopers and AT-ACTs on the

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:50.060
beach while carrying the tapes.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:54.930
Remember in the final cut of the movie, K-2SO
dies inside the Citadel while Jyn and Cassian

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:58.970
are recovering the tape, but in this shot
from the Celebration sizzle, it looks like

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:03.710
Alan Tudyk, who played K-2SO, is running along
the beach in the background in his mo-cap

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:04.710
suit.

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:08.160
So, it could be that, originally, the snarky
droid didn't die or at least not in the way

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.960
we saw in the movie.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:13.740
These cut scenes could also suggest that the
team was going to physically deliver the plans

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:16.740
intially rather than transmit them via a satellite
link.

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:20.870
Or perhaps more likely, the transmission antenna
was located in a different position to the

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:24.830
Citadel where they recovered the tapes the
final movie, which meant the team had to run

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:26.730
across the beach to reach the tower.

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:30.510
By the way, notice how Jyn and Cassian have
their normal clothes on at this point rather

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:34.410
than their imperial disguises which seems
to add to the theory that much of the assault

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:37.600
on Scarif was reworked during reshoots.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:40.990
Other deleted scenes from the Scarif battle
include Stormtroopers marching through the

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:45.410
water, Krennic's badass scene where he lands
and walks through the water trailing his white

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:49.610
cloak behind him, and Bistan the space monkey's
scene where he's machine-gunning from the

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:52.490
inside of a Rebel ship seems to have been
cut back as well.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:58.370
Another victim of the reshoots was astromech
imperial droid C2-B5 who served in the Citadel

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:00.240
vault performing maintenance tasks.

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:05.460
C2-B5, also dubbed as "evil R2-D2" by fans
when the character was officially announced,

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:09.889
didn't get any significant screentime, but
had a blink-and-you'll-miss-it cameo scooting

00:06:09.889 --> 00:06:12.110
behind some Stormtroopers in the Citadel.

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:16.500
I wonder if they ever planned with this character
to play on how the Death Star plans are entrusted

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:20.170
to R2-D2, reversing it or mirroring it in
some way.

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:24.200
Although all the characters die at the end
of Rogue One, in the very first screenplay

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.350
they actually didn't.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:29.620
In fact, director Gareth Edwards says he kept
expecting to be asked to put in a scene where

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:32.760
Jyn and Cassian survive and are living on
another planet.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:36.660
However, Edwards added that LucasFilm and
Disney understood that because the characters

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:40.490
weren't in A New Hope, it made sense that
they shouldn't survive Rogue One.

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:45.060
As well as providing the motion capture and
voice for K-2SO, Alan Tudyk also filmed a

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:47.900
small live-action cameo as an imperial pilot.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:52.070
The pilot would have been credited as played
by Wray Nerely who is the actor's character

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:56.560
in the web series Con Man, however the scene
was cut, which Tudyk has joked is entirely

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:58.620
appropriate for his character in Con Man.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:03.430
By the way, K2 also had a joke cut from the
trailers where he goes up to Jyn and declares

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:06.530
"the captain says you are a friend, I will
not kill you".

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:11.310
There's an intriguing deleted cameo in Rogue
One by model and actress Eunice Olumide who

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:15.669
filmed a scene on Jedha as a rebellion leader,
where she runs through a bar chased by a tank

00:07:15.669 --> 00:07:16.730
and Stormtroopers.

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:20.910
In the scene, she's wearing what she described
as a "really outlandish costume [and a] sort

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:22.170
of mushroom on [her] head."

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:26.080
And there's been speculation that her character
might have been Ahsoka Tano, who's featured

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:30.600
in both the animated Star Wars TV shows The
Clone Wars and Rebels.

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:35.070
Han Solo directors Phil Lord and Chris Miller
almost made it into Rogue One with cameos

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:37.420
in scenes that were meant to be part of the
Jedha sequence.

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:41.320
However, due to timing conflicts, they weren't
able to attend the shoot.

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:46.370
Star Wars fans can't forget Leia's famous
nerf herder insult to Han Solo in The Empire

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:50.680
Strikes Back and it looks like the original
script for Rogue One planned to introduce

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:53.889
actual nerf herders for the first time in
the Star Wars movies.

00:07:53.889 --> 00:07:59.370
Sadly, they didn't make it to the big screen,
but they were likely going to appear on Eadu.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:03.270
Concept art for the movie also reveals numerous
deleted characters and locations from Rogue

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:04.270
One.

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:08.880
On Jedha, there were Stormtroopers that rode
these incredibly tall camel-like animals.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:12.550
And Krennic even had an office set up on Jedha
in early concept art.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:16.330
Also there's some omitted backstory and characters
that would have explained what fugitive surgeon

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:18.570
Cornelius Evazan was doing on Jedha.

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:23.130
The headless humanoid Caysin Bog was hinted
at in the trailers, but we didn't get to see

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:28.960
the strange-looking servants called the Decraniated
who Evazan created during his various operations

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:30.050
in Jedha.

00:08:30.050 --> 00:08:36.289
Saw Gerrera had a medical droid called G2-1B7
which he used to help keep himself alive.

00:08:36.289 --> 00:08:41.080
There were imperial droids scurrying around
the core tower in the Scarif Citadel that

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:44.870
would have caused problems for Jyn trying
to access the data tapes.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:48.540
And there was going to be a mountain planet
where the inner Death Star dish was hidden.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:52.920
The dish would have risen out of a lake on
the planet to attach itself to the Death Star,

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:55.380
but the whole concept was scrapped for being
too complicated.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:59.540
And there was a bunch of other stuff from
the trailers that didn't make it in as well.

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:02.500
Take a look at some of it here and if you
have any theories on what it means let me

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:03.500
know below!

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:07.380
On Jedha there are a group of Rebel pilots
who've been taken prisoner and are being marched

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:12.400
along by Stormtroopers, and in another shot
Jyn hands something to the girl who she later

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:14.810
saves during the Partisan attack on the Stormtroopers.

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:18.990
There's a scene with Jyn sitting in the front
of Cassian's ship, a hologram of the Death

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:23.370
Star that pops up at the Rebel Base on Yavin
4, and finally we never got to see this very

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:26.610
cool iconic shot of Jyn in her imperial combat
suit.

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:30.080
So guys, what do you think about the deleted
scenes and reshoots?

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:33.060
Are there any deleted characters you'd like
to have seen in the movie?

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:35.400
I'd love to hear your thoughts in the comments
below.

